---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { FRESH_DAYS, STALE_DAYS } from '../lib/meta';
---

<Base title="About" description="How 850 Sip & Charge Map collects and checks its coffee shop Wi-Fi and outlet info.">
  <article class="container prose">
    <h1>About this map</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      850 Sip &amp; Charge Map helps Pensacola locals find a coffee shop where you can actually get work done: good
      Wi-Fi, a free outlet, and a table you can stay at for a while.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the info comes from</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>OpenStreetMap.</strong> The starting list of shops, locations and hours comes from the open map anyone can edit.</li>
      <li><strong>Locals.</strong> Tips shared in Pensacola community groups and reports on this site. We summarize what people say and never publish names.</li>
      <li><strong>Shop websites and public guides.</strong> Every shop page lists its sources and dates so you can judge for yourself.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How fresh is it?</h2>
    <p>Every shop shows when a person last confirmed its Wi-Fi and outlet details:</p>
    <ul class="legend">
      <li><span class="pill good"><span class="dot"></span>Verified</span> Confirmed in the last {FRESH_DAYS} days.</li>
      <li><span class="pill warn"><span class="dot"></span>Getting old</span> {FRESH_DAYS}–{STALE_DAYS} days ago.</li>
      <li><span class="pill"><span class="dot"></span>Needs a check</span> More than {STALE_DAYS} days ago.</li>
      <li><span class="pill"><span class="dot"></span>Unverified</span> From a listing or guide, not yet confirmed by a local.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>FAQ</h2>
    <h3>Do you list Wi-Fi passwords?</h3>
    <p>No. We only say whether there is a password and how to get it (ask staff, on your receipt, posted in store). Shops change them, and it is their call to share.</p>

    <h3>Is this official info from the shops?</h3>
    <p>No. It is a community project, not affiliated with any shop. Policies like "no laptops on weekends" change, so check in person.</p>

    <h3>Why isn't my favorite spot here?</h3>
    <p>We are just getting started in Pensacola. Drive-thru-only spots and places on base are left out on purpose. Everything else is fair game: tell us about it.</p>

    <h3>How do I report a change?</h3>
    <p>A quick report form on every shop page is on the way. Until then, mention <strong>850 Sip &amp; Charge</strong> in a local Pensacola Facebook group.</p>

    <h2>Credits</h2>
    <p>
      Map data © <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap contributors</a>. Map tiles by
      <a href="https://openfreemap.org">OpenFreeMap</a>. Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> and
      <a href="https://maplibre.org">MapLibre</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    margin-top: 2em;
  }

  .prose h3 {
    margin-top: 1.4em;
    margin-bottom: 0.3em;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .prose ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
  }

  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .legend {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0 !important;
  }

  .legend .pill {
    margin-right: 8px;
    min-width: 118px;
  }
</style>
